<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/008X">Exercise <span data-tag="008X">2.2.5.2</span>.</a> Check that the composition of lax functors is well-defined. That is, if $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ and $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ are lax functors between bicategories, then the identity and composition constraints $\epsilon ^{GF}_{X}$ and $\mu ^{GF}_{g,f}$ of Construction <a data-tag="008W" href="/tag/008W">2.2.5.1</a> are compatible with the unit constraints and associativity constraints of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, as required by Definition <a data-tag="008K" href="/tag/008K">2.2.4.5</a>. </p>
